'''Trevor Anthony Ariza''' (born June 30, 1985) is an American former professional [[basketball]] player who spent 18 seasons in the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). A small forward, Ariza played [[college basketball]] for one season with the [[UCLA Bruins men's basketball|UCLA Bruins]] before being selected in the second round of the [[2004 NBA draft]] by the [[New York Knicks]]. Ariza won an [[NBA championship]] with the [[Los Angeles Lakers]] in 2009. He also played for the [[Orlando Magic]], [[Houston Rockets]], [[New Orleans Pelicans|New Orleans Hornets]], [[Washington Wizards]], [[Phoenix Suns]], [[Sacramento Kings]], [[Portland Trail Blazers]], and [[Miami Heat]].

